    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0604" n="530" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg530"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.51/874</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commercial Adviser of the British Embassy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Crawford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        the Treasury</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McAdoo</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 29, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Ambassador’s note of
                    May 3 last,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d442-f1"/> I now have the honour to apply for
                    an advance of $185,000,000 to <pb facs="0605" n="531" xml:id="pg531"/> cover the
                    requirements of my Government in the United States for the month of June.</p>
                <p>I would suggest that the advance should be made in two instalments, $100,000,000
                    on the 10th of June and the remaining $85,000,000 on the 25th of June.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Crawford</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
